From 3c6cdd775340d036ab2ed6b1b4ff0fead3dd32a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:56:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Explain ops: a model change can't reuse consent that
 names another maker (306 fix e)

With Explain on and the consent naming xAI, deploy MODEL=sonnet55 set
Model=sonnet55 and Explain=on, and the workflow restored the switch to
on: visitors' sentences went to Anthropic under consent naming xAI. The
approval summary never named the model.

- ops.sh deploy: if the stack exists, Explain is on and its Model differs
  from the selected one, stop before any change ("Run pause first,
  publish consent and privacy for the new model, then deploy").
- ops.sh deploy, resume (switch on) and evaluate: while the site's
  published settings (site/data/explain.json, SITE_CONTRACT section 1)
  have "api" set, stop before signing in if the selected model isn't the
  published "model". No file, or "api" null, means no Explain control
  and no consent to contradict.
- summary.sh names the selected model and its maker for deploy, resume
  and evaluate, and says when the run will stop; it warns if no model was
  passed. model-table.mjs --name KEY gives "Grok 4.7, made by xAI".
- .github/workflows/explain.yml passes MODEL to the summary step. This
  is a protected path: the owner reviews and merges it.
- SITE_CONTRACT section 11 says what is now enforced.

Regressions (infra/aws/test_scripts.py): the 306 sequence (on with
Grok, prepare, deploy sonnet55, restore on) now stops and leaves Grok;
deploy, resume and evaluate refuse a model the published consent doesn't
name, with no AWS call; the summary names the model and the stop, and
warns when the model isn't passed; the workflow passes MODEL. These fail
on 19eebb3's scripts. Guards kept: a model change while off, and a
published file with api null, don't block. Infra 110 passed (ShellCheck
included); cfn-lint clean; model table check passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
